== ARCHIVE: the 38-member wheel (seven test modules), not-slow subset run outside the source tree ==

Object under test:
  nlcsplit-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl  SHA-256 55033716eb9b104a8aeb0d27b6fca0e39cab7e7b249e094ae39d2e69cbe9e911 (the build produced by the export
  run whose thirteen fatal gates came back empty)
  wheel members 38, seven test modules plus conftest.py and __init__.py, zero .pyc.
  Against the previous build (37 members, six test modules) the only additions are this
  test module and the refactor of nlcsplit/step_m_ccsdt.py.

Install: pip3 install --no-deps --target <dir>, then PYTHONPATH=<dir> with the working
directory inside <dir>, so nothing on sys.path is the repository.

    $ pytest --pyargs nlcsplit --collect-only -q
    49 tests collected
    $ pytest --pyargs nlcsplit -m "not slow" -q
    30 passed, 1 skipped, 18 deselected in 25.72s

(The first execution of the same subset, minutes earlier, reported 25.25 s.)

49 collected = 31 under `not slow` + 18 under `slow`. The single skip is the designed one:
test_geometry.py passes without the S22 official geometry download.

The 18 slow tests were not re-run on this wheel, and the carry-over is checkable rather
than assumed: the eight test files they live in are byte-identical to the ones on the
37-member wheel that was run in full at 2026-09-30T20:54Z (44 passed, 1 skipped -
`20260930T220142Z_wheel_pyargs_45_member37.out`), and `git diff --name-only afdefba HEAD --
nlcsplit/` shows that no library module they import changed since; the only paths added
under nlcsplit/ are step_m_ccsdt.py and the new test_cc_convention.py, and step_m_ccsdt.py
is imported only by the new test. Re-running the 18 would cost ~8 minutes to re-measure
unchanged code, so it is stated as a carry-over instead of performed and quietly implied.

Collection counts are the point of this log, not wall clock: 322 s, 505 s and 25 s have
been measured for overlapping subsets of the same suite under different thread settings
and different degrees of machine load, and none of them is "the" wheel test time.

